WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.470 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  sony pictures lifted the review embargo  for its highly anticipated anti-hero  flick  venom on tuesday october 2nd ahead of  its october 5th release date granting  permission to the fortunate few who saw  the film at its world premiere in los  angeles to post their spoiler-free  thought  in other words the reviews are in and  they're weird  bottom line many critics thought it was  hilarious but not quite on purpose  and that it features an unwelcome  throwback feel as if the mcu comic book  movie renaissance never happened the  hollywood reporters todd mccarthy for  example  thinks that venom is more black sheep  than black panther  writing venom feels like a throwback a  poor second cousin to the all-stars that  have reliably dominated the box office  charts for most of the century  there's a silver lining however tom  hardy collider's perry nimrod found  hardy typically charming as eddie brock  but wished the film had more of an  edge writing significant chunks of venom  don't work at all but there is some  serious charm to the eddie venom  relationship not sure i had the intended  reactions to some scenes but  fun is fun even when it's totally  ridiculous right it's too bad they  didn't go for the r rating though  nerdist hector navarro felt much the  same but pointed out that the film kept  true to the source material and  portraying eddie as a guy with an  off-kilter sense of humor  writing despite some problems venom did  right by its main character  people forget that he's always had a  weird sense of humor in the comics and  that humor is fully on display in the  movie  the verge's brian bishop wrote that  hardy gave a fully fleshed out  capital p performance as venom writing  hardy is always watchable no matter the  role but there's so much to take in here  that it almost feels like he's putting  on a one-man show  echoing that sentiment uprock's senior  entertainment writer mike ryan said he  was quote  fascinated with venom mostly because  while the rest of the cast was in a dark  superhero movie  hardy was decidedly not ryan tweeted  hardy is basically remaking jim carrey's  liar liar i kind of loved watching this  movie in a rocky horror type of way  oh i have a parasite yeah  my name is chen one of the harshest  reactions to venom came from ign's tom  jorgensen who wrote  sorry to say that venom is pretty much a  complete failure a tonal mess that feels  15 years old ignoring the storytelling  strides that the superhero genre has  made in recent years  mcu cosmic's jeremy conrad kept his  critique simple but  biting sharing a tweet that references  part of a line venom snarls in one of  the film's trailers  freelance comics journalist meg downey  delivered perhaps the most  interesting response to venom calling it  an excruciatingly surreal experience and  likening it to ben  affleck's daredevil english hulk and  halle berry's catwoman not  exactly great company downey wrote in  one tweet the humor the story beats  everything right down to the eminem  theme song  feels like it emerged kimmy schmidt  style from a sealed off early aughts  bunker  all in all the reviews indicate that  viewer mileage will vary wildly with  venom putting it just ahead of other  franchises non-starters like the  disastrous universal outing of the mummy  but owen gleberman a variety thinks it  might not be enough  this gateway into the sony universe of  marvel characters may not sputter as  badly as tom cruise is the mummy but it  could turn out to be a similar case of a  franchise kickoff that doesn't fully  attain franchise liftoff but if it does  well enough at the box office the  planned venom trilogy could indeed  become a reality  and all signs indicate the franchise is  primed to improve with each installment  leading up to fingers crossed a  potential spider-man crossover  or at least a substantial appearance by  venom's rival carnage if  and spoiler alert those early reports  about the mid-credits scene prove  correct  make your own call october 5th when  venom hits theaters nationwide

